# edge_ai_server_v90_multiuav.py -- Layer 2 Edge AI Server (Multi-UAV Extension)
#
# Changes over v85_adaptive:
#   [MU-1]  --zone-id CLI arg (default 1). Identifies this instance's zone.
#   [MU-2]  --coordinator-host / --coordinator-port CLI args.
#           All TRUST_HANDOVER outbound calls go to the coordinator, not to the
#           peer edge directly.  The coordinator routes to the correct target zone.
#   [MU-3]  TRUST_HANDOVER_LOAD inbound handler.
#           Pre-seeds per-CID state (speed hist, ts hist, safe_wins, llm_feedback,
#           ban/warn streaks, confirmed_banned_set) from inherited payload.
#           Responds with JSON ACK so coordinator knows the load succeeded.
#   [MU-4]  TRUST_HANDOVER_TRIGGER inbound handler.
#           NS3 sends this when a car reaches x = L - HANDOVER_LEAD_M.
#           Edge builds the TRUST_HANDOVER JSON from local state and forwards
#           to coordinator.  NS3 never talks to the coordinator directly.
#   [MU-5]  send_trust_handover() — assembles and sends TRUST_HANDOVER JSON
#           to coordinator:COORD_PORT.  Called by TRUST_HANDOVER_TRIGGER handler.
#   [MU-6]  send_overlap_score() — when a CID that arrived via TRUST_HANDOVER_LOAD
#           is scored by this edge, an OVERLAP_SCORE message is sent to the
#           coordinator so it can log cross-zone consensus.
#   [MU-7]  RESET handler extended to clear _handover_state and _overlap_cids.
#   [MU-8]  save_config_snapshot() and startup banner show ZONE_ID.
#   [MU-9]  tcp_call_framed() helper (same pattern as trust_coordinator.py).
#
# All v85 logic is completely preserved.  Multi-UAV additions are contained
# in clearly marked [MU-*] blocks.
# =============================================================================

